  "summary": "zyto 0.2.1 wheel installs a.pth startup hook absent from the sdist",
  "details": "The wheel distribution of zyto 0.2.1 installs a top-level zyto.pth file into site-packages containing `import zyto._hook; zyto._hook.fire_once()`. Python processes.pth lines that begin with `import` at every interpreter startup, so this code runs for any Python process on a machine where the wheel is installed, regardless of whether the user imports zyto. The.pth file is present only in the wheel and does not appear in the sdist, so the auto-execute behavior is wheel-specific and is the default on Linux x86_64/aarch64, Alpine, macOS arm64/x86_64, and Windows x86_64. The behavior of zyto._hook.fire_once() could not be traced from the provided evidence.",
